<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Computational Complexity Analysis</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a detailed computational complexity analysis for each phase of our PoLAR-VBLL framework, demonstrating its efficiency compared to alternative approaches for uncertainty quantification in fine-tuned LLMs.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Training Phase Complexity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The joint optimization of PoLAR adapter parameters <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Psi}_{\text{polar}}:=\{\mathbf{U},\boldsymbol{\Lambda},\mathbf{V}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚿</mi><mtext>polar</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Psi}_{\text{polar}}:=\{\mathbf{U},\boldsymbol{\Lambda},\mathbf{V}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and variational parameters <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Psi}=\{\boldsymbol{\mu}_{1},\ldots,\boldsymbol{\mu}_{C},\mathbf{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{S}_{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Psi}=\{\boldsymbol{\mu}_{1},\ldots,\boldsymbol{\mu}_{C},\mathbf{S}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{S}_{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math> involves the following computational costs per training iteration:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feature Extraction:</span> Computing LLM features <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{W}_{0}+\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{W}_{0}+\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for a batch of size <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(B\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(B\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}})</annotation></semantics></math> operations, where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the computational cost of a single forward pass through the base language model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PoLAR Parameter Updates:</span> The landing field optimization on Stiefel manifolds incurs:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Euclidean Gradient Calculation:
<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(mnr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(mnr)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Riemannian gradient computation: <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}r+n^{2}r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}r+n^{2}r)</annotation></semantics></math> for skew-symmetric operations <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Constraint gradient computation: <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((m+n)r^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((m+n)r^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for infeasibility penalties <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla N(\mathbf{U})=4\mathbf{U}(\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{U}-\mathbf{I}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla N(\mathbf{U})=4\mathbf{U}(\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{U}-\mathbf{I}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla N(\mathbf{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla N(\mathbf{V})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter updates: <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(r(m+n+r))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(r(m+n+r))</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> updates via landing field method</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VBLL Parameter Updates:</span> Variational inference optimization requires:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ELBO computation: <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(B\cdot C\cdot d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(B\cdot C\cdot d)</annotation></semantics></math> for likelihood terms and log-sum-exp operations in Eq. <a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.2 Fine-Tuned LLM via Orthogonalized LoRA ‣ 3 Variational Training of LLM-based Bayesian Last Layer Model via Orthogonal Low-Rank Adaptation ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KL divergence computation: <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for trace and determinant operations in covariance matrices <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gradient computation: <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for gradients with respect to variational means <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariances <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter updates: <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(B\cdot C\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(B\cdot C\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for updating <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> class-specific posterior distributions</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The total complexity per training iteration is:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(B\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}+r(m^{2}+n^{2})+B\cdot C\cdot d^{2}+r(m+n+r)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(B\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}+r(m^{2}+n^{2})+B\cdot C\cdot d^{2}+r(m+n+r)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> training iterations, the overall training complexity becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(T\cdot\left(B\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}+r(m^{2}+n^{2})+B\cdot C\cdot d^{2}+r(m+n+r)\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(T\cdot\left(B\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}+r(m^{2}+n^{2})+B\cdot C\cdot d^{2}+r(m+n+r)\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Predictive Inference Complexity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The uncertainty-aware prediction phase involves:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Optional Laplace Calibration:</span> Computing the Hessian of the negative log-likelihood for posterior refinement requires <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> operations using Kronecker-factored approximation (KFAC), which is significantly more efficient than the naive <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((C\cdot d)^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((C\cdot d)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> full Hessian computation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Monte Carlo Sampling:</span> For <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> posterior samples from <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parameter sampling: <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(K\cdot C\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(K\cdot C\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for sampling from multivariate Gaussians <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c},\mathbf{S}_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c},\mathbf{S}_{c})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Forward computation: <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(K\cdot C\cdot d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(K\cdot C\cdot d)</annotation></semantics></math> for logit computation <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\boldsymbol{\Theta}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\boldsymbol{\Theta}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and softmax normalization</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Total inference complexity per test point:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}+C\cdot d^{2}+K\cdot C\cdot d^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}}+C\cdot d^{2}+K\cdot C\cdot d^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Comparison with Baseline Methods</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vs. Standard LoRA:</span> Our PoLAR parameterization adds <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(r^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(r^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> overhead per update compared to LoRA’s <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(r)</annotation></semantics></math> due to orthogonality constraints, but this is negligible when <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\ll d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\ll d</annotation></semantics></math> while providing substantially improved stable rank utilization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vs. BLoB:</span> BLoB requires expensive Monte Carlo sampling during training with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N_{\text{MC}}\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N_{\text{MC}}\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}})</annotation></semantics></math> cost per ELBO evaluation, where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{MC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{MC}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of Monte Carlo samples. Our VBLL approach achieves analytical ELBO computation, eliminating this sampling overhead.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vs. Ensemble Methods:</span> Maintaining <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> separate adapter copies requires <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(M\cdot r(m+n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(M\cdot r(m+n))</annotation></semantics></math> storage and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(M\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mtext>cost</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(M\cdot\text{LLM}_{\text{cost}})</annotation></semantics></math> inference time. Our Bayesian approach achieves comparable uncertainty quality with <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(C\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> additional parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vs. Laplace-LoRA:</span> Post-hoc Laplace approximation around suboptimal MAP estimates requires similar Hessian computation but lacks the joint optimization benefits of our integrated approach.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Memory Complexity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The space complexity of our framework is:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(|\mathbf{W}_{0}|+r(m+n+r)+C\cdot d^{2}+B\cdot d\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(|\mathbf{W}_{0}|+r(m+n+r)+C\cdot d^{2}+B\cdot d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{W}_{0}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{W}_{0}|</annotation></semantics></math> represents the frozen pre-trained model size, <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(m+n+r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(m+n+r)</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for PoLAR parameters, <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\cdot d^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\cdot d^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> stores VBLL covariance matrices, and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\cdot d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\cdot d</annotation></semantics></math> handles intermediate feature storage during batch processing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Detailed Algorithm Specifications</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> PoLAR-VBLL Training </figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Pre-trained LLM weights <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, training dataset <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(\mathbf{x}_{n},{\bf y}_{n})\}_{n=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(\mathbf{x}_{n},{\bf y}_{n})\}_{n=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, rank <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, hyperparameters <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{\text{polar}},\eta_{\text{vbll}},\lambda,\sigma_{\theta}^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mtext>polar</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mtext>vbll</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{\text{polar}},\eta_{\text{vbll}},\lambda,\sigma_{\theta}^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Converged PoLAR parameters <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\mathbf{U}},\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}},\hat{\mathbf{V}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\mathbf{U}},\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}},\hat{\mathbf{V}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, variational posterior <math id="alg1.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{0}\in\text{St}(m,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>St</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{0}\in\text{St}(m,r)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{0}\in\text{St}(n,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>St</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{0}\in\text{St}(n,r)</annotation></semantics></math> via QR decomposition of random matrices

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},0.01^{2}\mathbf{I}_{r\times r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mn>0.01</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},0.01^{2}\mathbf{I}_{r\times r})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             Initialize VBLL parameters: <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,0}=\mathbf{w}_{\text{pretrain},c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mtext>pretrain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,0}=\mathbf{w}_{\text{pretrain},c}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{c,0}=\sigma_{\theta}^{2}\mathbf{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{c,0}=\sigma_{\theta}^{2}\mathbf{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1,\ldots,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1,\ldots,C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,1,\ldots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,1,\ldots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample mini-batch <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{t}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{t}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Extract features: <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{n})=\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}_{0}+\mathbf{U}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}^{\top}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{n})=\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}_{0}+\mathbf{U}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}^{\top}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{n}\in\mathcal{B}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{n}\in\mathcal{B}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute ELBO: <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}(\boldsymbol{\Psi}_{\text{polar}},\boldsymbol{\Psi};\mathcal{B}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚿</mi><mtext>polar</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}(\boldsymbol{\Psi}_{\text{polar}},\boldsymbol{\Psi};\mathcal{B}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. <a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.2 Fine-Tuned LLM via Orthogonalized LoRA ‣ 3 Variational Training of LLM-based Bayesian Last Layer Model via Orthogonal Low-Rank Adaptation ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              // PoLAR parameter updates via landing field method

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute weight gradient: <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}_{t}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial(\mathbf{U}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}^{\top})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}_{t}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial(\mathbf{U}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}^{\top})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute factor gradients:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbf{U}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{G}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbf{U}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{G}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbf{G}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbf{G}_{t}\mathbf{V}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbf{G}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{U}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}=\mathbf{G}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{U}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute Riemannian gradients:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U}_{t})=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{U}_{t}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U}_{t})=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{U}_{t}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V}_{t})=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{V}_{t}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V}_{t})=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}_{t}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{V}_{t}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
              Landing field updates:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Gamma}(\mathbf{U}_{t})=\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U}_{t})\mathbf{U}_{t}+\lambda\cdot 4\mathbf{U}_{t}(\mathbf{U}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{U}_{t}-\mathbf{I}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Gamma}(\mathbf{U}_{t})=\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U}_{t})\mathbf{U}_{t}+\lambda\cdot 4\mathbf{U}_{t}(\mathbf{U}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{U}_{t}-\mathbf{I}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
