</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l31.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span> <math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{U}}=\mathbf{U}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{U}}=\mathbf{U}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}=\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}=\boldsymbol{\Lambda}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l32.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{V}}=\mathbf{V}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{V}}=\mathbf{V}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})=\prod_{c=1}^{C}\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c};\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,T},\mathbf{S}_{c,T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})=\prod_{c=1}^{C}\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c};\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,T},\mathbf{S}_{c,T})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Uncertainty-Aware Prediction in PoLAR-VBLL</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Converged PoLAR parameters <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\mathbf{U}},\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}},\hat{\mathbf{V}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\mathbf{U}},\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}},\hat{\mathbf{V}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, variational posterior <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\boldsymbol{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, test input <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, training data <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of samples <math id="alg2.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, Laplace refinement flag

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
              
             Predictive distribution <math id="alg2.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y^{*}|\mathbf{x}^{*},\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y^{*}|\mathbf{x}^{*},\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> Laplace refinement enabled <span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
              // Optional posterior refinement via Laplace approximation

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute converged means: <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{c}=\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{c}=\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,T}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1,\ldots,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1,\ldots,C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute Hessian using KFAC approximation:

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{c}=-\nabla^{2}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}}\left(\log p(\mathcal{D}|\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c},\hat{\boldsymbol{\Psi}}_{\text{polar}})+\log p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})\right)\Big\rvert_{\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}=\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>polar</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{c}=-\nabla^{2}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}}\left(\log p(\mathcal{D}|\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c},\hat{\boldsymbol{\Psi}}_{\text{polar}})+\log p(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})\right)\Big\rvert_{\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}=\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Form Laplace posterior: <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})=\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c};\hat{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{c},\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})=\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c};\hat{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_{c},\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_{c}=\mathbf{H}_{c}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_{c}=\mathbf{H}_{c}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="alg2.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1,\ldots,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1,\ldots,C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
             // Extract test features

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}^{*}=\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}_{0}+\hat{\mathbf{U}}\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}\hat{\mathbf{V}}^{\top}}(\mathbf{x}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}^{*}=\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}_{0}+\hat{\mathbf{U}}\hat{\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}\hat{\mathbf{V}}^{\top}}(\mathbf{x}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
             // Monte Carlo sampling for predictive distribution

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
             Initialize prediction accumulator: <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}=\mathbf{0}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}=\mathbf{0}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> Laplace refinement enabled <span id="alg2.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               Sample classification weights: <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}^{(k)}\sim q_{\text{Lap}}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext>Lap</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}^{(k)}\sim q_{\text{Lap}}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1,\ldots,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1,\ldots,C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
               Sample classification weights: <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}^{(k)}\sim q(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})=\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,T},\mathbf{S}_{c,T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c}^{(k)}\sim q(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{c})=\mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c,T},\mathbf{S}_{c,T})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1,\ldots,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1,\ldots,C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
              Form weight matrix: <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{(k)}=[\boldsymbol{\theta}_{1}^{(k)},\ldots,\boldsymbol{\theta}_{C}^{(k)}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{(k)}=[\boldsymbol{\theta}_{1}^{(k)},\ldots,\boldsymbol{\theta}_{C}^{(k)}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute logits: <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{(k)}=\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{(k)}\boldsymbol{\phi}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{(k)}=\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{(k)}\boldsymbol{\phi}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute sample prediction: <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}^{(k)}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}^{(k)}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{z}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
              Accumulate: <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}=\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}+\mathbf{p}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}=\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}+\mathbf{p}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
              
              
             Average predictions: <math id="alg2.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y^{*}|\mathbf{x}^{*},\mathcal{D})=\frac{1}{K}\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y^{*}|\mathbf{x}^{*},\mathcal{D})=\frac{1}{K}\mathbf{p}_{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span> Predictive distribution <math id="alg2.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y^{*}|\mathbf{x}^{*},\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y^{*}|\mathbf{x}^{*},\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Detailed Gradient Derivations</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the complete derivation of gradient updates for the joint PoLAR-VBLL optimization procedure described in Section 3.2.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.1 </span>Variational Parameter Updates</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The gradients with respect to the variational parameters <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c},\mathbf{S}_{c}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c},\mathbf{S}_{c}\}</annotation></semantics></math> follow standard variational inference procedures:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\left[y_{n,c}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})-\frac{\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{c}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}{\sum_{j=1}^{C}\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{j}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{j}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\left[y_{n,c}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})-\frac{\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{c}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}{\sum_{j=1}^{C}\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{j}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{j}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{1}{\sigma_{\theta}^{2}}\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{1}{\sigma_{\theta}^{2}}\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial\mathbf{S}_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial\mathbf{S}_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\left[-\frac{\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{c}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}{\sum_{j=1}^{C}\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{j}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{j}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\left[-\frac{\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{c}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{c}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}{\sum_{j=1}^{C}\exp(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{j}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})+\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\mathbf{S}_{j}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n}))}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x}_{n})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{\theta}^{2}}\mathbf{I}_{d}+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{S}_{c}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{\theta}^{2}}\mathbf{I}_{d}+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{S}_{c}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.2 </span>PoLAR Parameter Updates</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the PoLAR parameters, we employ the chain rule to propagate gradients through the feature extractor <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\mathbf{W}}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{W}_{0}+\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{W}_{0}+\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}:=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial(\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}:=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial(\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top})}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the gradient with respect to the weight update. Then:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}}{\partial\boldsymbol{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{G}\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{G}\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{G}\mathbf{V}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐆𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{G}\mathbf{V}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{G}^{\top}\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{G}^{\top}\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.3 </span>Riemannian Gradient Computation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math> are constrained to Stiefel manifolds, we convert the Euclidean gradients to their Riemannian counterparts. For a matrix <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\in\text{St}(m,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>St</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\in\text{St}(m,r)</annotation></semantics></math>, the Riemannian gradient is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{grad}_{R}f(\mathbf{X})=\nabla f(\mathbf{X})-\mathbf{X}\nabla f(\mathbf{X})^{\top}\mathbf{X}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>grad</mtext><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{grad}_{R}f(\mathbf{X})=\nabla f(\mathbf{X})-\mathbf{X}\nabla f(\mathbf{X})^{\top}\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Applying this to our PoLAR parameters:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{U}^{\top})=\text{Skew}(\mathbf{G}\mathbf{V}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}^{\top}\mathbf{U}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐆𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{U}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{U}^{\top})=\text{Skew}(\mathbf{G}\mathbf{V}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}^{\top}\mathbf{U}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{V}^{\top})=\text{Skew}(\mathbf{G}^{\top}\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Skew}(\nabla_{\mathbf{V}}\mathcal{L}^{\text{ELBO}}\cdot\mathbf{V}^{\top})=\text{Skew}(\mathbf{G}^{\top}\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Skew}(\mathbf{A})=\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{A}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Skew</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Skew}(\mathbf{A})=\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{A}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math> extracts the skew-symmetric component.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.4 </span>Landing Field Updates</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the infeasible optimization approach, we replace the expensive retraction operations with landing field updates:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\Gamma}(\mathbf{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\Gamma}(\mathbf{U})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U})\mathbf{U}+\lambda\nabla N(\mathbf{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{U})\mathbf{U}+\lambda\nabla N(\mathbf{U})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\Gamma}(\mathbf{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\Gamma}(\mathbf{V})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V})\mathbf{V}+\lambda\nabla N(\mathbf{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{V})\mathbf{V}+\lambda\nabla N(\mathbf{V})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla N(\mathbf{U})=4\mathbf{U}(\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{U}-\mathbf{I}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla N(\mathbf{U})=4\mathbf{U}(\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{U}-\mathbf{I}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla N(\mathbf{V})=4\mathbf{V}(\mathbf{V}^{\top}\mathbf{V}-\mathbf{I}_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla N(\mathbf{V})=4\mathbf{V}(\mathbf{V}^{\top}\mathbf{V}-\mathbf{I}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> are the gradients of the infeasibility penalties <math id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(\mathbf{U})=\|\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{U}-\mathbf{I}_{r}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(\mathbf{U})=\|\mathbf{U}^{\top}\mathbf{U}-\mathbf{I}_{r}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(\mathbf{V})=\|\mathbf{V}^{\top}\mathbf{V}-\mathbf{I}_{r}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(\mathbf{V})=\|\mathbf{V}^{\top}\mathbf{V}-\mathbf{I}_{r}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The complete update procedure alternates between updating the variational parameters using standard gradient-based optimizers (e.g., Adam) on Eqs. <a href="#A1.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ A.6.1 Variational Parameter Updates ‣ A.6 Detailed Gradient Derivations ‣ Appendix A Computational Complexity Analysis ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>–<a href="#A1.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ A.6.1 Variational Parameter Updates ‣ A.6 Detailed Gradient Derivations ‣ Appendix A Computational Complexity Analysis ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>, and updating the PoLAR parameters using the landing field approach on Eqs. <a href="#A1.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ A.6.2 PoLAR Parameter Updates ‣ A.6 Detailed Gradient Derivations ‣ Appendix A Computational Complexity Analysis ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ A.6.4 Landing Field Updates ‣ A.6 Detailed Gradient Derivations ‣ Appendix A Computational Complexity Analysis ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ A.6.4 Landing Field Updates ‣ A.6 Detailed Gradient Derivations ‣ Appendix A Computational Complexity Analysis ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Training Settings</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model Architecture.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our implementation builds upon the <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LlaMA-3.1-8B</span> and <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLaMA-2-7B</span> foundation models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, utilizing its pre-trained language modeling head for VBLL mean initialization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PoLAR Configuration.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The manifold penalty coefficient in PoLAR <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. We parameterize the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix using the identity initialization and apply Landing Field optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lion et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schechtman et al., 2023</a>)</cite> with gradient type set to ”landing”. The Landing Field callback is enabled during training to maintain stability in optimization on the Grassmann manifold.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VBLL Parameterization.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For VBLL, we adopt the dense parameterization for computational efficiency while maintaining uncertainty quantification capabilities. The Jensen bound is used for approximating the softmax function. Prior hyperparameters are set as follows: prior scale <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta}^{2}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta}^{2}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, Wishart scale <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{0}=10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{0}=10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, degrees of freedom <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The regularization weight for KL divergence is computed as <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{reg}}=1/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>reg</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{reg}}=1/N</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the training set size. This regularization weight can be used to adjust the emphasis of model performance on ACC or Uncertainty Quantification ability. All parameter values are the default classification setting in the VBLL library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harrison et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Configuration.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all shared parameters, we follow the settings of BLoB’s official single-GPU scripts, except for LoRA Rank and LoRA Alpha, to ease BNN training and improve performance.
We train all methods (PoLAR-VBLL and baselines) for 5000 training steps with a batch size of 4, evaluation batch size of 8, and maximum sequence length of 300 tokens. All methods use AdamW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov and Hutter, 2017</a>)</cite> optimizers with learning rate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and a CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts scheduler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov and Hutter, 2016</a>)</cite>.
Baselines are reproduced strictly according to the implementations in their official repositories. For sampling-based methods (BLoB, TFB, ScalaBL, C-LoRA), we set training sampling <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{train}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{train}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (single sample per forward pass) and inference sampling <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{eval}}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{eval}}=10</annotation></semantics></math>. LoRA/PoLAR rank (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=8</annotation></semantics></math>), alpha (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=16</annotation></semantics></math>), and dropout (0.0). All training is conducted in BF16 precision on CUDA devices. For all MC-based uncertainty quantification evaluations, we use <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{samples}}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>samples</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{samples}}=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LA Calibration.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For post-hoc calibration, we apply LA with a diagonal Hessian structure over all model parameters. The prior precision is set to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation of PoLAR-ized Variants.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adapt existing Bayesian LoRA methods to PoLAR by applying uncertainty quantification specifically to the core matrix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> while preserving the Stiefel manifold constraints on the orthogonal factors <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PoLAR-BLoB</span> replaces standard LoRA with the PoLAR parameterization <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{V}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and applies variational inference to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, learning a diagonal covariance for the approximate posterior <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\boldsymbol{\Lambda}|\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\boldsymbol{\Lambda}|\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math> during training while keeping <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}\in\text{St}(m,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>St</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}\in\text{St}(m,r)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}\in\text{St}(n,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>St</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}\in\text{St}(n,r)</annotation></semantics></math> deterministic.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PoLAR-LA</span> performs MAP estimation on all PoLAR parameters <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{U},\boldsymbol{\Lambda},\mathbf{V}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{U},\boldsymbol{\Lambda},\mathbf{V}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then computes the Laplace approximation by estimating the Hessian with respect to the adapter parameters at the MAP solution. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PoLAR-LA-LL</span> applies LA only to the last (classification) layer for direct comparison with our VBLL framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PoLAR-TFB</span> applies training-free Bayesianization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite> by performing SVD on the trained core matrix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and inferring the posterior covariance scale <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> via binary search on a held-out anchor set. However, despite our best efforts, we cannot find a proper set of hyperparameters to yield competitive performance.
We hypothesize that TFB’s covariance estimation, originally designed for the full low-rank factors in standard LoRA, may not transfer effectively to the compact <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times r</annotation></semantics></math> core matrix in PoLAR. We therefore omit PoLAR-TFB and PoLAR-TFB-LL from our comparisons.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Computational Environment</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hardware Specifications.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted on a high-performance computing system equipped with NVIDIA RTX A6000 Ada GPUs and AMD 9600 Threadripper processors with 64 cores and 128 threads. This configuration provides substantial computational resources for both GPU-accelerated training and CPU-intensive operations such as Hessian computation for Laplace approximation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Software Dependencies.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our implementation leverages several key Python packages: PyTorch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke, 2019</a>)</cite> for deep learning operations, HuggingFace PEFT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mangrulkar et al., 2022</a>)</cite> for adapter implementations, custom Laplace approximation libraries <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daxberger et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kristiadi et al., 2024</a>)</cite> for post-hoc uncertainty calibration, PoLAR optimization libraries <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lion et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and VBLL (Variational Bayesian Last Layer) implementations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harrison et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Complete dependency specifications and version information are provided in our <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">requirements.txt</span> file, which will be made available upon acceptance.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Extend Experiments</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Additional Backbone Evaluation on LlaMA-2-7B</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted comprehensive experiments on <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LlaMA-2-7B</span> across four datasets with all baseline methods. As shown in Table <a href="#A3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ C.1 Additional Backbone Evaluation on LlaMA-2-7B ‣ Appendix C Extend Experiments ‣ Scalable Variational Bayesian Fine-Tuning of LLMs via Orthogonalized Low-Rank Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, BLoB exhibits a trade-off between accuracy and uncertainty quantification: at <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=0</annotation></semantics></math> sampling, it achieves higher accuracy but with reduced calibration quality; as sampling increases to <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math>, BLoB shows improved uncertainty metrics but with degraded predictive accuracy. In contrast, our PoLAR-VBLL framework achieves competitive accuracy across all datasets while maintaining strong uncertainty calibration, demonstrating that high predictive performance and well-calibrated uncertainties can be obtained simultaneously without requiring the typical trade-off. The optional LA refinement further enhances ECE and NLL while preserving accuracy, confirming that our variational training provides a robust foundation for posterior refinement. These results demonstrate that our framework generalizes effectively beyond <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LlaMA-3.1-8B</span>, consistently achieving superior uncertainty quantification while maintaining competitive predictive performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="A3.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performances on ID datasets in terms of ACC, ECE, and NLL using <span id="A3.T2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LlaMA2-7B</span>. Bold and underlined denote the best and the second-best performance, respectively. Here, we include PoLAR-VBLL with and without LA.</span></figcaption>
